body:
When adding a child to an entity that has sprite components, sometimes the entity and some (but not always all) of it's parents become invisible, adding further children sometimes resolves this, but not permanently.

Here's the code that I'm using to get this, there is a single red square in the center on startup:

In full disclosure, the 2D camera I'm using has been zoomed in (`scale = 1.0 / 80.0`), and had it's `far = 1000.0 / scale`.

```rust
struct ChildMarker;

 fn add_children(
     mut commands: Commands,
     keys: Res<Input<KeyCode>>,
     mut mats: ResMut<Assets<ColorMaterial>>,
     mut query: Query<Without<ChildMarker, (Entity, &Sprite)>>)
 {
     if keys.just_pressed(KeyCode::C)
     {
         for (entity, _) in &mut query.iter()
         {
             let child = commands
                 .spawn(SpriteComponents
                 {
                     sprite: Sprite { size: Vec2::new(1.0, 1.0), },
                     draw: Draw
                     {
                         is_transparent: true,
                         ..Default::default()
                     },
                     material: mats.add(ColorMaterial::color(
                         Color::rgba(0.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0.25))),
                     translation: Translation::new(-0.5, -0.5, 0.1),
                     ..Default::default()
                 })
                 .current_entity()
                 .unwrap();

             commands.push_children(entity, &[child]);

             commands.insert_one(entity, ChildMarker);
         }
     }
 }
```


![examples](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20546688/93268691-9de09280-f77b-11ea-9d6e-55fa5a4af8b7.png) Above are some images that show what's happening. You can clearly see when some squares are missing, and that they re-appear later.
